{
  "_why": "Role track for INJECTION MOULDING, a new pack for an already-declared kind (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Phase 2 #9, sheet 22). `injection_moulding_operator` was declared in Batch 3 for its vocabulary; this is its first pack. fam_injection_moulding binds the four NCO plastic-moulding occupations (8142.0501 Injection Moulding Machine Operator, 8142.0502 Moulding Operator, 8142.1300 Mould Setter, 8142.1301 Plastic Moulding Technician or Operator) at job-domain specificity 50; every other 814 code stays on fam_rubber_plastic.",
  "_scope": "THE MOULDING MACHINE, NOT THE TOOL ROOM. A man who builds the mould (core, cavity, spotting, tryout) is a Tool & Die Maker; this trade runs, sets and optimises the injection moulding machine the mould is hung on. 'mould ka kaam / die ka kaam' stays an ask-first disambiguation (A3), never a route.",
  "_depth": "THE TIER GATE IS moulding_experience, asked FIRST (the descriptor's tenureQuestionKey). Its options carry value_number ONLY: pack-registry.service.ts resolves valueText ?? valueNumber, and a value_text would turn every gte below into a string compare that is false forever (the #776 defect).",
  "_budget": "MAX_ENGINE_ASKS is 28 and qp_universal spends 8. Easy is 2 trade items + at most 1 confirm; Medium adds 2 (brand, tonnage); Advanced adds 4 (material, process work, defects, training). Worst case 2 + 1 + 2 + 4 = 9 trade asks.",
  "_sheet": "READ OFF CEO LAUNCH PLAN PACK v1 SHEET 22 (no ratified page). Section title 'Moulding, machines & capability'. Its rows are Brands, Tonnage, Materials, Work, Defects and Training, and every row has exactly one question here.",
  "pack_id": "qp_injection_moulding",
  "version": 1,
  "family_id": "fam_injection_moulding",
  "locale": "hi-IN",
  "status": "active",
  "review_note": "v1 (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Phase 2 #9): first pack for the declared kind injection_moulding_operator. Easy/Medium/Advanced tiers; 6-band experience; sheet-22 level ladder (Trainee/Operator/Setter/Senior (process technician)/Supervisor, mandatory); 2 separating confirms, both the sheet's questions verbatim: setter, and senior; supervisor by rule. Medium Q6 machine brand, Q7 tonnage; Advanced Q9 materials, Q10 process depth, Q11 defects handled, Q12 the ITI/CIPET training row (tool-room institute-row precedent), depth rows gated years OR rung. Deviations recorded: tonnage is a single 'up to' band (press-shop precedent); the sheet's 'Other' chips are the 'Inme se koi nahi' escape; no fresher items and no shared ITI block beyond Q12 (new-trade precedent). Drafted for owner review (Prakash).",
